{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines","id":611069,"title":"new editions for other gamelines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-01T10:54:44-07:00","id":611069,"title":"new editions for other gamelines?","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> With the announcment that vtm is getting a 4th edition what does that mean for the other game lines? should we expect to see werewolf and mage 4th editions in the future, not sure if that would be needed, but it is a question to be asked? what of wraith and changeling? To be honest I kind of thought that the 20th versions were a new edition of sorts. I haven't played much vtm recently but I thought they would be getting new supplements for the 20th line?<br /> <br /> So should there be a new edition for the other game lines?<br /> <br /> ~herkles~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:12:37-07:00","id":611091,"title":"","content":"Well, M20 has some serious metaplot &quot;options&quot; that may benefit from some exploring. And I think that Demon can benefit from some extra material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:51:56-07:00","id":611120,"title":"","content":"The option will be useful for those of us who can't afford $100 on a 600-page compendium of material they already have (in V20's case).<br /> <br /> I imagine the metaplot will follow the one suggested in the recent MRev Convention Books. So I think Mage will get one too. Changeling and Wraith would need third editions first, of course. Unless OPP opts to have the 20th Anniversary Editions be their revised editions too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:10:19-07:00","id":611131,"title":"","content":"Wr20 is already the equivalent of the Revised book we never got, and contains options for moving the metaplot. I don't see any need there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:32:02-07:00","id":611206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=611131#post611131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wr20 is already the equivalent of the Revised book we never got, and contains options for moving the metaplot. I don't see any need there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess few people would right now, but things can always change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:06:21-07:00","id":611256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=611120#post611120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The option will be useful for those of us who can't afford $100 on a 600-page compendium of material they already have (in V20's case).<br /> <br /> I imagine the metaplot will follow the one suggested in the recent MRev Convention Books. So I think Mage will get one too. Changeling and Wraith would need third editions first, of course. Unless OPP opts to have the 20th Anniversary Editions be their revised editions too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they'd try forcing all the games to be 4th editions, myself, just having new editions regardless of the numbering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:20:31-07:00","id":611272,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't see any <i>need</i> for 4th edition books. I mean I won't turn them down, I guess. But to be perfectly honest, I'm happy with the 20th anniversary stuff (the art in some of the werewolf products notwithstanding... fuckin' Melvin the Minotaur...)<br /> <br /> But then, I'm mostly a Werewolf player, and Werewolf has never really had the enameled layers of metaplot that Vampire, mage, or even changeling (my other game) had. It's always been way more &quot;sandbox&quot; and so if the idea of 4th edition is to update metaplot... well, again. Happy with W20, thanks! Maybe release an eratta booklet for any system updates, but really, that's all that's needed.<br /> <br /> M20 was, and Wr20 / C20 probably will be, large enough overhauls and modern-era updates to their original systems that a 4th (...3rd?) edition for them will not be needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:25:53-07:00","id":611274,"title":"","content":"i think werewolf could use new mechanics from combat to make the forms relevant to streamline the regeneration but is nothing i cant house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:47:06-07:00","id":611285,"title":"","content":"I'd expect the the Onyx Path folks are certainly putting 4th Editions for the whole cWOD in their minds.<br /> <br /> However, I'd also say they're not going to commit to it too much until after VtM 4e gets released. Just like V20's successes lead to the full 20th line getting going, I'd imaging 4e cWOD is going to hinge heavily on how well VtM starts things off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:39:17-07:00","id":611670,"title":"","content":"I would love to see demon get a new addition, I might even be able to either resurrect my old group or start a new group in Jax Fl if it did","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T13:29:16-07:00","id":612538,"title":"","content":"Really, the 20th anniversary books pretty much -are- 4th editions in some, if not all regards. There is modernization of metaplot and theme here and there, rule tweaks, more things put into the core books...I am not sure how a '4th edition' would differ from what we got.<br /> <br /> The previous editions didn't overhaul everything there was, though of course the transition from 1st to 2nd tended to always have the biggest changes due to the developers gaining experience and feedback.<br /> <br /> Though, I agree. Hunter, Demon and Mummy 20th Anniversary editions would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T21:38:28-07:00","id":613011,"title":"","content":"Demon was release in 2002, we'd have to wait till 2022 for a 20th Anniversary edition... so, I'd say a Revised Edition is a better option.<br /> <br /> IMHO DtF is the best cWoD line not called Vampire, but it's rules require a serious overhaul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1119,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","user":"Primal Flame","date":". 08-03-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T23:52:00-07:00","id":613058,"title":"","content":"I agree in that another edition it's probably a better option. Not so much for the time, but because the published material wasn't <i>that big</i>.<br /> I think Demon doesn't need a compilation. But more Demon would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T08:40:34-07:00","id":613390,"title":"","content":"I'm super jazzed about Wr20. I would love to see a Hunter: the Reckoning 20th, too. Perhaps they could work out some of the problems between what the game actually was and what the art always showed. There were only a few of the Creeds that were about wrecking the monsters all the time and even then they probably weren't able to just hack, slash, and blast their way though a whole horde of zombies on their own. So, restating what the game is actually about and making sure this is readily visible to the casual observer would go a very long way toward redeeming the Hunters (who happened to have a creed named Redeemers). Also, this one was really big on metaplot. I really would like to see where some of those storylines would have went had the line not needed to end in the Time of Judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T09:09:48-07:00","id":613474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=613058#post613058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much for the time, but because the published material wasn't <i>that big</i>.<br /> I think Demon doesn't need a compilation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this applies to most of the post &quot;First Five,&quot; cWOD lines. Hunter was probably the one with the most books of that group (24 not counting Apocrypha and published fiction). But the vast majority of its run was the core three (Core/ST Handbook/Players Guide), nine Creedbooks, and seven &quot;crossover&quot; books for the other game lines/existing monster hunting organizations.<br /> <br /> KotE clocked in at 17 books (also with a large portion of that being splat books). Demon hit 8, Mummy 2 (4 is you count the early edition ones before it became a separate game line), and Orpheus (which seems to be getting worked into Wr20 anyway) got its 6.<br /> <br /> Even if we were to get 20th edition books addressing those... HtR and KotE are the only two that you could even conceive of having 20th edition supplements for. The others should be simple to do in a 500+ page core tome for people that might want them while a brand new cWOD 4th edition is being worked on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:48:25-07:00","id":616067,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda confused what the point is of a 4th edition of anything considering the approach they have been having with the 20th Anniversary material and the huge list of supplements they are getting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T01:35:41-07:00","id":616085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=616067#post616067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda confused what the point is of a 4th edition of anything considering the approach they have been having with the 20th Anniversary material and the huge list of supplements they are getting.</div> </div> </div> </div>20th is a metaplot agnostic, toolkit approach to celebrate the classic line.<br /> <br /> 4th will update the metaplot from Revised and bring the classic game into the 21st century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T01:38:41-07:00","id":616089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=616067#post616067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda confused what the point is of a 4th edition of anything considering the approach they have been having with the 20th Anniversary material and the huge list of supplements they are getting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was confused about at first, too, but they released a long explaination on the newsletter/blog today.<br /> <br /> It seems that unlike, say, Mage 20 where the metaplot was pushed forward and rules were revised and changed, V20 Masquerade supposedly barely is anything but a collection of previous material. No big changes, no plot advancement. It -was- their first 20th Anniversary book, in their defense, when perhaps the idea of the 20th materials simply was to be all-in-one collections of core material, previous rules and factions. The following 20th releases more and more changed that, and V20 Masquerade now feels bland in comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:45:27-07:00","id":616607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=611272#post611272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't see any <i>need</i> for 4th edition books. I mean I won't turn them down, I guess. But to be perfectly honest, I'm happy with the 20th anniversary stuff (the art in some of the werewolf products notwithstanding... fuckin' Melvin the Minotaur...)<br /> <br /> But then, I'm mostly a Werewolf player, and Werewolf has never really had the enameled layers of metaplot that Vampire, mage, or even changeling (my other game) had. It's always been way more &amp;quot;sandbox&amp;quot; and so if the idea of 4th edition is to update metaplot... well, again. Happy with W20, thanks! Maybe release an eratta booklet for any system updates, but really, that's all that's needed.<br /> <br /> M20 was, and Wr20 / C20 probably will be, large enough overhauls and modern-era updates to their original systems that a 4th (...3rd?) edition for them will not be needed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Do elaborate The Melvin The Minotaur, please","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T09:28:11-07:00","id":617820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=616085#post616085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">20th is a metaplot agnostic, toolkit approach to celebrate the classic line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, as RichT said recently, <b>V20</b> was never meant as a Fourth Edition, but rather it was a compendium of all that had come before. Yeah, there was new art and some updated rules, but it didn't really contain much setting information and had a LOT of cut-and-paste from Revised Edition in it.<br /> <br /> <b>W20</b> and especially <b>M20</b> come much, much closer to being something like new editions of their respective games, but both (and again, especially <b>M20</b>) are unwieldy in terms of sheer page number/weight and the level of 'oh-my-f@ck that's too much information!' that appears in them for any new players to approach. <b>V20</b> wasn't meant to be so much a gaming book, though, as it was a straight up 'for the fans' kinda love letter. It was only after the mad success of the offering that Onyx Path was created, that CCP decided that yes, maybe the 'old' World of Darkness (now <i>Classic</i> World of Darkness) could be a viable set of products, and that anything like a <b>V20</b> line was created.<br /> <br /> ...From what I can tell, <b>V4</b> (nope, still don't like calling it that...) will be smaller than the '$100 and 600 page' <b>V20</b>, more approachable, AND will be a proper 21st Century game. I dunno what we'll get from this Fourth Edition of <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b>, but I have full confidence that it's gonna be brilliant. Of course, there's always a <i>chance</i> it will stink like ape balls, and in that case, I'll just have to fall back on <b>V20</b> and the three previous editions of <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b>, I guess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T10:38:32-07:00","id":617872,"title":"","content":"V20 is pretty perfect if you want to play the 'classic' game. So if they bugger up V4, I'm not so worried.<br /> <br /> I am also looking forward to V4 as a print book, as I simply can't afford $100 for a POD copy of V20 and miss having actual printed pages rather than a PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T17:08:43-07:00","id":618231,"title":"","content":"While I have moved onto NWoD and don't have much desire to play CWoD a lot again. I will say I would excited to see where the OP writers would take the Revised metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T08:50:54-07:00","id":618995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=616607#post616607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Do elaborate The Melvin The Minotaur, please</div> </div> </div> </div>The art for the Apis was pretty bad in CB20. As in, it didn't look like a bad ass minotaur but a middle-aged football fan who is also a bullman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T09:36:48-07:00","id":619023,"title":"","content":"On one hand, I'm afraid of cWoD turning into the nWoD. <br /> <br /> On the other, many changes were influenced by long time players and STs, and are definite improvements. (Newly changed and first rank werewolves not having to be teenagers being a big one. Incorporating that into the metaplot would be awesome.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T19:44:18-07:00","id":619690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=618995#post618995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The art for the Apis was pretty bad in CB20. As in, it didn't look like a bad ass minotaur but a middle-aged football fan who is also a bullman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't care for the Apia or the Camazotz art in all honesty. Most of the art in CB20 was good though. I don't mind a 4th version of the game I play Star Fleet Battles and trust me that is far worse for new updates or was. There are things that were not addressed in the 20 th Anniversary editions that could be handled in a new update.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T17:11:22-07:00","id":620730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/611069-new-editions-for-other-gamelines?p=619023#post619023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand, I'm afraid of cWoD turning into the nWoD.<br /> <br /> On the other, many changes were influenced by long time players and STs, and are definite improvements. (Newly changed and first rank werewolves not having to be teenagers being a big one. Incorporating that into the metaplot would be awesome.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you have nothing to worry about as the purpose of a new edition wont be to turn CWoD into NWoD at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T10:21:57-07:00","id":621442,"title":"","content":"if demon does get a new addition and gets revived I want to see books that show how demons react when they are in possession of bodies from religions other than abrahamic ones, I would love to see how a demon that subscribes to nordic religions views the world and prehistory and more options are always good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T03:41:40-07:00","id":625283,"title":"","content":"I hope Demon gets a revised. The powers could use a bit of tweaking to balance them out. I would also love to see a bit more side by side balance for all the supernatural types as my players all have a favorite and none of them are the same! The weres are the big integration issue as their ranks are pretty out of whack as far as lining up with most other things. <br /> Honestly if they just used a lot of the nWoD and did full books pulling in the cWoD would be great. Sure there are conversions but I'd rather spend the money for a book of pre-converted rules, looks better and goes quicker!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}